{
  "action": "After a standard system update you need to restart dnsmasq to make\nall the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-12725",
    "CVE-2026-12969"
  ],
  "description": "Yiwei Hou discovered that Dnsmasq incorrectly handled logging of DS or\nDNSKEY. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2026-12725)\n\nIt was discovered that Dnsmasq incorrectly validated the length of\nfixed-length DNS record fields when parsing NS section records. A remote\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause Dnsmasq to read out of\nbounds, possibly exposing sensitive information. (CVE-2026-12969)",
  "id": "USN-8542-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in Dnsmasq.",
